course: dictionary
lesson: 15836
title: Fair and unfair
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Undeserved means you did not earn it, or it is not fair. The word has two parts: un- means not, and deserved means earned. So undeserved means not earned.
explain: «Mia got an undeserved punishment for something her brother did.» Mia did nothing wrong, so the punishment was not fair. The clues are «for something her brother did» and the word undeserved itself.
explain: Undeserved can also describe good things. «The team's win was undeserved, because they had broken the rules.» The win was not earned, so it does not count as fair. Ask yourself: did this person earn it?
fact: Undeserved means not earned, or not fair.
fact: The prefix un- means not, and deserved means earned.
fact: «Undeserved punishment» means a punishment that was not fair.
fact: «Undeserved praise» means praise that was not earned.
fact: Undeservedly is the adverb: it means in a way that is not earned or fair.
exercise: «Mia got an undeserved punishment for something her brother did.» What does undeserved mean? | *Not fair, because she did not earn it | Well deserved and earned | Very fast | Very large
exercise: The hero received «undeserved praise». What does undeserved praise mean? | *Praise that was not earned | Praise written in a book | Praise given every day | Loud praise from the crowd
exercise: «The team's win was undeserved, because they had broken the rules.» Find and copy one word that means not earned. | *undeserved | rules | team | win
test: The villain had undeserved luck, so the reader felt cross. What does undeserved mean here? | *Not earned, so it was unfair | Quiet and calm | Lucky and earned | Very kind
test: Which word is the adverb of undeserved? | Undesired | *Undeservedly | Quickly | Deservingly
exam: Which sentence shows an undeserved reward? | Ben cleaned the whole kitchen and was thanked | *Ben did no work but was given a prize anyway | Ben read a book | Ben tidied his room
